vttest -- the VT100 compatibility test======================================    vttestA menu of tests for a terminal that claims to be a VT100: cursormovement, screen features (scrolling regions, attributes, tabs), thecharacter sets, double-width and double-height lines, the keyboard, theterminal's answers to status requests, VT52 mode, the VT102 insert anddelete features, known bugs, and reset.  Type a test's number and RETURN;each page says what a correct terminal shows, and RETURN moves on.  0leaves.It is a tool for judging a terminal, so the answer depends on the terminal:run it on the screen or serial terminal you want to test.  The keyboardand reports tests read what the terminal sends back.By Per Lindberg, Stockholm University Computing Center, 1983-85, ascomp.sources.unix posted it.  Full originals in SRC/vttest/ORIG.